# Cursor Rules for T3 Project

## Code Style & Module System
- Use ES modules (import/export) instead of CommonJS (require/module.exports)
- Use .js extension for standalone scripts
- Use TypeScript for all source files (.ts/.tsx)
- Prefer modern JavaScript features and syntax

## Project Structure
- This is a full-stack TypeScript project with:
  - Backend: Node.js/Express server in `/src`
  - Frontend: Next.js React app in `/client`
- Use existing patterns and conventions from the codebase
- Follow the established folder structure

## Dependencies & Tools
- Use npm for package management
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Use existing UI components from `/client/src/components/ui`

## Code Quality
- Write clean, readable code with proper TypeScript types
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Follow existing error handling patterns
- Use the established authentication and middleware patterns

## File Naming
- Use kebab-case for files and directories
- Use PascalCase for React components
- Use camelCase for functions and variables
- Use UPPER_CASE for constants

## When creating new files:
- Always use ES modules syntax
- Include proper TypeScript types
- Follow the existing project structure
- Use existing patterns from similar files in the codebase
